{
  "id": "perceptual-neglect",
  "term": "perceptual neglect",
  "definition": "Perceptual neglect here refers to a reduced tendency to perceive the overall, whole shape of a visual pattern, especially when it is shown in peripheral vision, while more local elements are more readily seen. In the source packet, this pattern is described as peripheral global perceptual neglect, with central vision not showing the same reduction.",
